1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:06,000
National Radio and Television Administration

2
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:30,000
[Welcome to Sister Pang's Bathhouse]

3
00:02:00,480 --> 00:02:02,000
Isn't there a surveillance camera?

4
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,160
If we pull up the footage from that day,

5
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:04,620
we'll know what happened.

6
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:06,000
Uncle.

7
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:07,560
This is a murder case.

8
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:08,560
The police have already taken the videos

9
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:10,560
from before and after the incident.

10
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:30,120
I've always felt that

11
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:35,300
it was only a matter of time before someone like my brother got killed.

12
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:38,450
I just didn't expect

13
00:02:40,320 --> 00:02:43,040
that he would actually end up like this.

14
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:44,960
Don't be too sad.

15
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:48,840
Why would I be sad?

16
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:53,420
Ever since I can remember,

17
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:58,840
my dad would beat my brother whenever he was upset.

18
00:02:59,120 --> 00:03:00,840
And my brother was so stubborn,

19
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:03,120
he never knew how to beg for mercy.

20
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:06,120
I don't know where he got such a temper.

21
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:06,650
You know,

22
00:03:06,880 --> 00:03:09,120
he was always getting into fights outside

23
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:10,250
and never came home.

24
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:14,020
In the end, he started going to jail time and time again.

25
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:17,490
The villagers never stopped gossiping about it.

26
00:03:18,920 --> 00:03:21,780
It made our whole family unable to hold our heads up.

27
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:24,560
The last time he was in prison,

28
00:03:25,480 --> 00:03:27,040
my mom died of an illness.

29
00:03:28,720 --> 00:03:31,079
She died calling his name.

30
00:03:32,960 --> 00:03:34,360
Even when the old lady was dying,

31
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:36,490
she couldn't stop worrying about him.

32
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:39,840
Since then, my dad stopped contacting him

33
00:03:40,079 --> 00:03:43,079
and even moved us away on purpose.

34
00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:44,079
Well...

35
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:45,760
I... I want this money,

36
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:47,240
but not for myself.

37
00:03:47,960 --> 00:03:50,840
You see, my dad is getting old

38
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:52,100
and his health is poor.

39
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:55,240
The house needs to be repaired too.

40
00:03:58,680 --> 00:03:59,520
This money,

41
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:06,490
just consider it my brother fulfilling his filial duty.

42
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:10,760
I understand.

43
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:13,460
Anyway, regarding the money,

44
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:17,240
I will definitely try my best to fight for it.

45
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:19,459
Brother Hu,

46
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:21,970
come with me on a field assignment.

47
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:25,080
Didn't you say we can't review the files?

48
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:27,400
Then how do you know where the murderer lives?

49
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:30,280
The cause, process, and related evidence of the case

50
00:04:30,280 --> 00:04:31,880
cannot be reviewed right now.

51
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:33,800
But the personal information of the parties involved

52
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:35,360
can still be found.

53
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:46,440
Hello.

54
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:52,159
Hello. Is anyone there?

55
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:53,850
What do you want?

56
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:54,320
Hello.

57
00:04:54,320 --> 00:04:57,080
We are looking for Fu Xiaochen's relatives.

58
00:05:00,680 --> 00:05:02,200
Who are you?

59
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:15,000
Have some water, comrades.

60
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:15,600
Thank you.

61
00:05:16,600 --> 00:05:17,080
Thank you.

62
00:05:17,080 --> 00:05:18,010
Have some water.

63
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:23,320
It's fine.

64
00:05:23,440 --> 00:05:25,320
The old man is hard of hearing.

65
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:26,800
Lawyer.

66
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:28,920
You see, we went out to work before.

67
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:33,040
We got a little work injury and can't do heavy labor anymore.

68
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:34,760
The old man is getting old,

69
00:05:34,760 --> 00:05:36,620
so we came back to take care of him.

70
00:05:37,159 --> 00:05:38,800
We didn't make any money,

71
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:42,200
and we didn't raise our child well either.

72
00:05:42,200 --> 00:05:43,200
Our Xiaochen,

73
00:05:43,880 --> 00:05:45,720
although his grades were not good,

74
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:47,920
he is a very honest child.

75
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:50,120
He is also filial to his grandmother.

76
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:51,200
After graduating from technical school,

77
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:53,659
he worked on a construction site in the city.

78
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:56,200
He even sent money back to us.

79
00:05:56,760 --> 00:06:01,440
A child like him who hasn't even killed a chicken or a duck,

80
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:04,490
how could he get into this kind of trouble?

81
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:07,640
Lawyer, I know you must pay a life for a life.

82
00:06:07,920 --> 00:06:11,120
Will my son be

83
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:14,520
executed?

84
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:21,000
I can't say for sure.

85
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:22,200
I came here today

86
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:24,120
to represent the victim's family.

87
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:25,640
Let's talk about this.

88
00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:27,240
What the family means is that

89
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:30,880
if you are willing to pay some compensation,

90
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:33,440
you can get their forgiveness.

91
00:06:35,120 --> 00:06:36,120
Forgiveness?

92
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:37,760
It means that

93
00:06:37,840 --> 00:06:39,640
after you pay the compensation,

94
00:06:39,840 --> 00:06:42,800
you can get a letter of forgiveness from the victim's family.

95
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:44,040
This letter of forgiveness

96
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:45,800
for Xiaochen's sentencing

97
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:46,840
is very important.

98
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:47,400
Well...

99
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:49,960
We are willing to.

100
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:51,040
We are willing to pay.

101
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:51,600
We are willing to pay.

102
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:54,440
Xiaochen's father happens to have some work injury compensation.

103
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:55,840
We are willing to give it.

104
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:57,320
If it's not enough, I'll borrow some.

105
00:06:57,320 --> 00:06:58,520
As long as I can save my son,

106
00:06:58,520 --> 00:07:00,050
I can even give them my life.

107
00:07:00,400 --> 00:07:02,730
Please talk to their family nicely, okay?

108
00:07:02,840 --> 00:07:04,160
I beg you, lawyer.

109
00:07:04,440 --> 00:07:05,970
Please talk to them nicely.

110
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:10,360
As a serious and rigorous

111
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:11,280
Legal worker.

112
00:07:11,280 --> 00:07:13,340
I want to discuss a question with you.

113
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:14,320
Look.

114
00:07:14,320 --> 00:07:15,600
Suppose there is a person

115
00:07:15,600 --> 00:07:16,600
who is very poor.

116
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:18,480
If he kills someone,

117
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:20,520
he doesn't have the money to pay compensation.

118
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:21,520
Does that mean he can only

119
00:07:21,520 --> 00:07:22,680
honestly wait

120
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:23,880
for whatever sentence he gets?

121
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:25,120
On the other hand,

122
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:26,040
suppose there is a person

123
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:27,440
who is not short of money at all.

124
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:29,360
Does that mean he can kill whoever he wants?

125
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:30,720
Anyway, when the time comes,

126
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:32,280
the worst that can happen is he pays compensation

127
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:34,400
and then spends a dozen years in prison.

128
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:35,280
The way this works

129
00:07:35,280 --> 00:07:37,080
is like opening a back door for the rich.

130
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:38,810
I think it's extremely unfair.

131
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:41,620
If you think like that,

132
00:07:41,680 --> 00:07:43,320
you're being a bit extreme.

133
00:07:43,320 --> 00:07:45,680
The circumstances of each case are different.

134
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:49,010
You have to see if the circumstances of the crime are severe,

135
00:07:49,120 --> 00:07:50,680
and if its impact is huge.

136
00:07:50,840 --> 00:07:51,760
Besides,

137
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:53,840
the purpose of punishment is not

138
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:54,600
to penalize,

139
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:55,880
but to reform.

140
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,800
Paying compensation is just one of the ways of repentance

141
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:01,520
recognized by the law.

142
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:03,090
If you don't have money,

143
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:04,440
there are other ways.

144
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:06,000
I get the gist of it.

145
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,560
Let's get back to this case.

146
00:08:07,640 --> 00:08:09,680
If Fu Xiaochen is really a

147
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:11,760
very obedient and sensible child,

148
00:08:11,880 --> 00:08:13,960
and when he encountered that incident,

149
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:15,000
he panicked

150
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:16,840
and took extreme actions,

151
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:18,050
and afterwards,

152
00:08:18,120 --> 00:08:19,240
he is willing to repent

153
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:20,500
and pay compensation,

154
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:24,520
then the court can certainly handle it at its discretion.

155
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:27,160
That's not right.

156
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:28,240
Logically speaking,

157
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:30,240
shouldn't you be more familiar with Zhao Deqing?

158
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:31,440
What you're implying

159
00:08:31,440 --> 00:08:33,100
is all in favor of Fu Xiaochen.

160
00:08:35,520 --> 00:08:36,980
I'm not familiar with him.

161
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:41,049
Understood.

162
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:52,200
It's the middle of the night.

163
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:53,720
Are you trying to scare people by pretending to be a ghost?

164
00:08:53,720 --> 00:08:56,320
Did you go talk to someone about compensation?

165
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:57,160
Yes.

166
00:08:58,080 --> 00:08:58,720
No.

167
00:08:59,360 --> 00:09:01,420
Didn't I introduce Zhao Deyan to you?

168
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:05,330
I'm telling you, Xiaolong. What are you doing...

169
00:09:07,080 --> 00:09:08,080
Hello, Ms. Zhao.

170
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:10,800
I've already met Fu Xiaochen's parents.

171
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:13,480
They are quite willing to pay compensation.

172
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:15,760
Anyway, let's find another time to discuss it.

173
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:19,490
Once the amount is confirmed, we can issue a letter of forgiveness.

174
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:22,920
It's the least I could do.

175
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:23,640
Okay.

176
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:10,440
My butt hurts.

177
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:11,760
Brother Jun.

178
00:10:12,160 --> 00:10:13,760
This is the first time you're treating me to a meal.

179
00:10:13,760 --> 00:10:15,800
Is it okay that we didn't bring Xiao Longnv?

180
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:16,720
I see her every day.

181
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:17,920
Why would I bring her?

182
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:19,280
Okay.

183
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:21,120
As long as you think it's fine.

184
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:22,080
Come on, let's go.

185
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:22,740
Here we are.

186
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:24,920
I was thinking about etiquette

187
00:10:24,920 --> 00:10:25,920
and stuff like that.

188
00:10:25,920 --> 00:10:26,850
Come on, come on.

189
00:10:26,880 --> 00:10:27,520
No, no, you first.

190
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:28,320
Come on, go in.

191
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:29,280
After you. Go in. Please.

192
00:10:29,280 --> 00:10:30,520
You're too kind, Brother Jun.

193
00:10:30,520 --> 00:10:31,520
Come on, hurry up.

194
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:42,040
No, Brother Jun, this...

195
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:48,120
Brother Jun, what kind of meal is this?

196
00:10:48,120 --> 00:10:49,780
Why do we have to lock the door?

197
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:53,440
It's just these guys.

198
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:54,000
I don't need to introduce them.

199
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,600
You know who they are, right?

200
00:10:55,640 --> 00:10:57,640
Are these the legendary Eight Great Guardians?

201
00:10:57,640 --> 00:10:59,280
As long as you behave,

202
00:10:59,280 --> 00:11:00,810
I guarantee you'll be fine.

203
00:11:03,600 --> 00:11:04,360
Well...

204
00:11:04,760 --> 00:11:06,160
Including you, there are only five.

205
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:07,440
Three are missing.

206
00:11:07,840 --> 00:11:09,360
Two are dead.

207
00:11:09,400 --> 00:11:11,520
And one had a stroke and can't get out of bed.

208
00:11:11,520 --> 00:11:13,520
What? Why are you telling him that?

209
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:15,040
Come on.

210
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:16,480
Hurry up and eat.

211
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:17,680
So we can hit the road.

212
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:19,480
No, what road am I hitting?

213
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:20,960
What did I do, Brother Jun?

214
00:11:21,040 --> 00:11:21,480
I mean,

215
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:23,940
you'll lead us to Fu Xiaochen's house later.

216
00:11:24,920 --> 00:11:27,520
I remember the way to Fu Xiaochen's house.

217
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:30,480
But your daughter, Xiao Longnv, won't allow it.

218
00:11:34,520 --> 00:11:36,040
What era is this?

219
00:11:36,040 --> 00:11:37,000
Brothers,

220
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:38,160
I've grown up.

221
00:11:38,160 --> 00:11:39,040
This doesn't scare me anymore.

222
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:41,240
So you mean you don't want to lead us there?

223
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:41,640
How can I go?

224
00:11:41,640 --> 00:11:43,000
If you don't go, I'm telling you,

225
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,560
your life won't be peaceful anymore.

226
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:45,760
What else can happen?

227
00:11:45,880 --> 00:11:48,680
Fine, I'll rely on you for the rest of my life.

228
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:49,520
No, don't.

229
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:53,800
Okay, okay, I yield.

230
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:54,330
I give up.

231
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:55,360
I give up, okay?

232
00:11:56,760 --> 00:11:58,560
Okay, let's eat first.

233
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:11,700
What are you doing?

234
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:13,500
I thought we should all go.

235
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:25,280
What are you doing?

236
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:26,200
Stop right there!

237
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:27,400
I didn't do anything.

238
00:12:28,520 --> 00:12:29,200
Where are you going?

239
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:29,760
It's him.

240
00:12:29,760 --> 00:12:32,360
He's been sneaking around here for a long time.

241
00:12:32,760 --> 00:12:34,480
What are you guys doing?

242
00:12:34,480 --> 00:12:35,360
What do you mean sneaking around?

243
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:36,600
I'm tailing someone.

244
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:37,840
Tailing? Tailing who?

245
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:38,900
Explain yourself.

246
00:12:39,720 --> 00:12:41,240
You're not leaving until you explain.

247
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:42,320
Explain what?

248
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:43,840
You're even calling for backup.

249
00:12:43,840 --> 00:12:45,320
The police will be here soon.

250
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:46,720
I am the police.

251
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:48,610
Is this me? Look, come here.

252
00:12:51,760 --> 00:12:53,640
This place looks too fancy.

253
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:56,240
Sir, all your dishes are served. Enjoy your meal.

254
00:12:56,240 --> 00:12:56,840
Thank you.

255
00:12:57,120 --> 00:12:57,720
Lawyer Li,

256
00:12:57,880 --> 00:12:59,400
do you have some good news to announce?

257
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:00,560
Did you take on another big case?

258
00:13:00,560 --> 00:13:02,520
What? Can't we eat without taking a case?

259
00:13:02,520 --> 00:13:03,120
Come.

260
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:06,120
Thank you all for your recent dedication and hard work.

261
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:07,380
It's nothing. Cheers.

262
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:11,240
Let's eat.

263
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:12,720
I've always hoped

264
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:14,480
that we are a highly efficient team.

265
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:14,880
But...

266
00:13:17,640 --> 00:13:18,200
Hello?

267
00:13:21,560 --> 00:13:22,200
Okay, I got it.

268
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:23,260
I'll head over now.

269
00:13:23,360 --> 00:13:24,080
Listen, you guys eat.

270
00:13:24,080 --> 00:13:25,040
I'll go pay the bill.

271
00:13:25,040 --> 00:13:25,560
I have an emergency.

272
00:13:25,560 --> 00:13:26,320
In such a hurry?

273
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:27,440
Do you need me to go with you?

274
00:13:27,440 --> 00:13:28,040
No need.

275
00:13:32,800 --> 00:13:35,760
Didn't Lawyer Li say 'but' before he left?

276
00:13:38,520 --> 00:13:39,280
I knew it.

277
00:13:40,360 --> 00:13:42,120
This meal isn't as easy

278
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:43,000
as it looks.

279
00:13:43,200 --> 00:13:44,330
Something's wrong.

280
00:13:44,360 --> 00:13:47,120
I heard the firm recently recruited a group of newcomers.

281
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:48,520
They seem quite capable.

282
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:49,240
Who did you hear that from?

283
00:13:49,240 --> 00:13:51,640
Are they recruiting new colleagues for us?

284
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:55,840
He didn't say.

285
00:13:56,600 --> 00:13:58,660
Then they're not recruiting people.

286
00:13:59,360 --> 00:14:00,720
They're replacing people.

287
00:14:00,720 --> 00:14:01,640
Don't talk nonsense.

288
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:02,520
Are you crazy?

289
00:14:02,680 --> 00:14:04,920
We were all carefully selected by Lawyer Li,

290
00:14:04,920 --> 00:14:05,800
the elite.

291
00:14:05,920 --> 00:14:07,800
They can't replace us no matter what.

292
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:09,260
You two weren't selected.

293
00:14:09,360 --> 00:14:10,320
Not selected?

294
00:14:11,120 --> 00:14:12,320
Drawn by lots?

295
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:13,340
Leftovers.

296
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:14,600
Leftovers?

297
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:16,610
Lawyer Li was late that day.

298
00:14:16,840 --> 00:14:18,300
Everyone else was picked.

299
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:19,660
Only you two were left.

300
00:14:21,160 --> 00:14:22,890
Then this isn't a dinner party.

301
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:25,740
Isn't this a farewell dinner?

302
00:15:00,320 --> 00:15:02,920
A mosquito bit me under my thigh. It's so itchy.

303
00:15:03,560 --> 00:15:05,820
There are too many mosquitoes in summer.

304
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:11,280
Get some more sleep, Brother Jun.

305
00:15:11,280 --> 00:15:12,560
I'll wake you up when we arrive.

306
00:15:12,560 --> 00:15:13,080
No.

307
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:14,720
I really have a big bump here.

308
00:15:14,720 --> 00:15:15,640
Yes, no, I...

309
00:15:15,640 --> 00:15:16,360
Look. Look.

310
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:26,200
I'm not bullying you.

311
00:15:26,600 --> 00:15:27,960
The whole village is my relatives.

312
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:28,880
Right, right, right.

313
00:15:28,880 --> 00:15:30,280
Get out. Get out.

314
00:15:30,280 --> 00:15:31,480
What are you yelling about?

315
00:15:31,480 --> 00:15:33,520
A life for a life is perfectly justified.

316
00:15:33,520 --> 00:15:35,120
Don't think you can buy a life with money.

317
00:15:35,120 --> 00:15:35,520
Exactly.

318
00:15:35,520 --> 00:15:36,160
You know?

319
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:37,640
Money won't work.

320
00:15:37,920 --> 00:15:40,000
It's not for outsiders to meddle in our family's business.

321
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:41,320
Don't move. Don't move.

322
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:42,650
Don't move. Don't move.

323
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:44,320
Alright. Are you rebelling?

324
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:45,380
Alright. Alright.

325
00:15:45,400 --> 00:15:45,760
Alright.

326
00:15:45,760 --> 00:15:46,760
Listen to me.

327
00:15:48,720 --> 00:15:49,240
Let's not be impulsive.

328
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:50,700
Can't we just talk nicely?

329
00:15:50,720 --> 00:15:52,120
It's not worth it at your age.

330
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:55,000
You're the young man who came with the lawyer last time, right?

331
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:55,720
What do you want to do?

332
00:15:55,720 --> 00:15:56,440
Who are you trying to scare?

333
00:15:56,440 --> 00:15:57,200
Trying to raise the price?

334
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:58,520
Get out.

335
00:15:58,760 --> 00:15:59,490
Dare to move?

336
00:15:59,800 --> 00:16:00,640
Come on, make a move.

337
00:16:00,640 --> 00:16:01,280
Stop arguing.

338
00:16:01,280 --> 00:16:02,320
No, stop arguing.

339
00:16:03,360 --> 00:16:04,520
Alright, alright.

340
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:13,160
Touch my brother again. Just try it.

341
00:16:13,160 --> 00:16:13,960
Stop it.

342
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:18,040
Xiao Jun, Xiao Jun.

343
00:16:18,120 --> 00:16:18,920
Stop it.

344
00:16:21,040 --> 00:16:22,370
What are you doing here?

345
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:23,900
Are you guys together?

346
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:26,000
About the compensation issue,

347
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:27,480
they just don't understand.

348
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:29,200
It's fine. I'll take them away now.

349
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,000
Sorry.

350
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:30,480
Let's go.

351
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:32,000
What compensation?

352
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:34,770
Brother.

353
00:16:35,720 --> 00:16:38,520
Don't think we country folks don't know the law.

354
00:16:38,520 --> 00:16:41,040
The lawyer we hired has seen Xiaochen.

355
00:16:41,040 --> 00:16:43,240
He said Xiaochen works hard

356
00:16:43,240 --> 00:16:44,280
at the auto repair shop.

357
00:16:44,280 --> 00:16:46,040
It's Zhao Deqing's fault.

358
00:16:46,040 --> 00:16:49,000
Our Xiaochen acted in self-defense.

359
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:50,440
It's not a crime at all.

360
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:52,160
And we definitely won't pay compensation.

361
00:16:52,160 --> 00:16:53,220
Do you understand?

362
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:54,360
The lawyer said so.

363
00:16:54,360 --> 00:16:55,890
Right, Lawyer Qian said so.

364
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:57,360
Don't talk nonsense here.

365
00:16:57,360 --> 00:16:58,400
If murder is not a crime,

366
00:16:58,400 --> 00:16:59,160
then I am not guilty today.

367
00:16:59,160 --> 00:17:00,200
Stop spreading rumors here.

368
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:01,530
You are guilty. Stop it.

369
00:17:01,680 --> 00:17:02,080
Stop it. Come on.

370
00:17:02,080 --> 00:17:05,079
The police are here. The police are here.

371
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:07,000
Stop.

372
00:17:07,359 --> 00:17:08,890
It's a society ruled by law.

373
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:10,660
I've recorded all your faces.

374
00:17:10,680 --> 00:17:12,280
Who hit whom, how they hit,

375
00:17:12,280 --> 00:17:13,520
and what they used.

376
00:17:13,520 --> 00:17:14,720
I've recorded it all.

377
00:17:14,720 --> 00:17:17,640
These videos will be handed over to the police as evidence.

378
00:17:17,640 --> 00:17:19,000
Then you'll compensate as required

379
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:20,400
and be sentenced accordingly.

380
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:21,280
Understand?

381
00:17:21,640 --> 00:17:22,170
Let's go.

382
00:17:22,280 --> 00:17:24,940
Let's go. Are you waiting for a banquet? Go home.

383
00:17:26,760 --> 00:17:27,890
Don't be impulsive.

384
00:17:28,319 --> 00:17:28,880
Let's go.

385
00:17:30,040 --> 00:17:31,520
It has nothing to do with me.

386
00:17:31,520 --> 00:17:33,160
Get in the car. Get in the car.

387
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:40,400
[Sister Pang's Laundry]

388
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:42,760
Was the guy with Xiaolong just now

389
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:44,540
Director Li's son?

390
00:17:45,520 --> 00:17:46,920
He looks quite handsome.

391
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:48,040
Absolutely.

392
00:17:48,440 --> 00:17:49,480
He's a fine-looking young man.

393
00:17:49,480 --> 00:17:50,040
Yeah.

394
00:17:50,600 --> 00:17:52,400
He's a good match for our Xiaolong, isn't he?

395
00:17:52,400 --> 00:17:53,240
For sure.

396
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:55,400
Look at the car he drives.

397
00:17:56,240 --> 00:17:57,240
A Mercedes-Benz.

398
00:17:57,520 --> 00:17:59,920
Do you know there's an excellent quality called keeping a low profile?

399
00:17:59,920 --> 00:18:00,920
Give me a break.

400
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:02,520
What's so great about driving an automatic?

401
00:18:02,520 --> 00:18:03,680
My manual transmission

402
00:18:03,680 --> 00:18:06,080
is a man's ultimate control over a machine.

403
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:07,800
Give it a rest.

404
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:10,280
If you really like controlling machines,

405
00:18:10,280 --> 00:18:13,280
why don't you go tinker with machine tools in a factory?

406
00:18:13,280 --> 00:18:14,360
Exactly.

407
00:18:14,520 --> 00:18:16,040
He can afford to drive a nice car.

408
00:18:16,040 --> 00:18:17,240
Intentionally not driving it,

409
00:18:17,240 --> 00:18:18,900
that's what you call low-key.

410
00:18:19,160 --> 00:18:21,000
He's just talking nonsense.

411
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:22,280
If you're poor, just admit it.

412
00:18:22,280 --> 00:18:23,040
Right.

413
00:18:26,160 --> 00:18:26,760
Are you trying to murder us?

414
00:18:26,760 --> 00:18:27,760
What the hell are you doing?

415
00:18:27,760 --> 00:18:28,240
Did you do that on purpose?

416
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:28,760
No, no.

417
00:18:28,760 --> 00:18:30,760
Look at you guys, you're over 200 years old combined.

418
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:31,640
Why so suspicious?

419
00:18:31,640 --> 00:18:33,300
There's a pothole on the road.

420
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:46,160
Why did you go make such a scene?

421
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:47,600
What good did it do?

422
00:18:47,600 --> 00:18:48,880
I served as a warning.

423
00:18:49,240 --> 00:18:50,160
I let them know that from now on,

424
00:18:50,160 --> 00:18:52,040
they shouldn't dream of settling things with money.

425
00:18:52,040 --> 00:18:53,520
And what's this about self-defense?

426
00:18:53,520 --> 00:18:54,360
That was intentional homicide.

427
00:18:54,360 --> 00:18:55,840
Do you even know what intentional homicide

428
00:18:55,840 --> 00:18:56,920
or self-defense is?

429
00:18:56,920 --> 00:18:58,120
You just say whatever comes to mind.

430
00:18:58,120 --> 00:18:59,720
How old are you, Dad?

431
00:18:59,720 --> 00:19:01,240
Still fighting and killing?

432
00:19:01,240 --> 00:19:02,720
Didn't you tell me

433
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:05,120
that the underworld is about worldly wisdom,

434
00:19:05,120 --> 00:19:06,160
not fighting and killing?

435
00:19:06,160 --> 00:19:07,160
What were you doing just now?

436
00:19:07,160 --> 00:19:08,120
Who were you going to kill or beat up?

437
00:19:08,120 --> 00:19:08,880
There was no fight.

438
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:10,480
What do you mean? Just drive.

439
00:19:11,080 --> 00:19:13,840
Besides, I don't know what kind of person Fu Xiaochen is,

440
00:19:13,840 --> 00:19:16,320
but we both know what Uncle Daqing is like.

441
00:19:17,160 --> 00:19:18,920
Would you have gone back to prison if it weren't for him?

442
00:19:18,920 --> 00:19:21,080
Xiaolong, your Uncle Daqing has changed for the better.

443
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:21,920
How do you know?

444
00:19:21,920 --> 00:19:22,960
You haven't contacted each other for over ten years.

445
00:19:22,960 --> 00:19:24,240
Did he tell you in a dream?

446
00:19:24,240 --> 00:19:26,160
You're just prejudiced against Uncle Daqing.

447
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:27,440
Do you even know him?

448
00:19:27,640 --> 00:19:29,160
He was a brother who would risk his life for me.

449
00:19:29,160 --> 00:19:30,400
Do you know how hard it hit me

450
00:19:30,400 --> 00:19:31,640
now that he's gone?

451
00:19:35,880 --> 00:19:37,200
You didn't say a single word of comfort to me.

452
00:19:37,200 --> 00:19:38,400
That doesn't matter.

453
00:19:38,480 --> 00:19:40,280
But can't you at least try

454
00:19:40,280 --> 00:19:41,480
to put yourself in my shoes?

455
00:19:41,480 --> 00:19:43,480
How am I not putting myself in your shoes?

456
00:19:43,480 --> 00:19:44,160
What else do you want me to think?

457
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:46,280
What do you think I'm working so hard for every day?

458
00:19:46,280 --> 00:19:47,240
Brothers who would risk their lives?

459
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:48,720
Those brothers of yours,

460
00:19:48,720 --> 00:19:50,320
especially Uncle Daqing...

461
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:51,880
That's enough.

462
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:52,640
Don't stop halfway.

463
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:53,400
He's gone now.

464
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:54,160
Say whatever you want.

465
00:19:54,160 --> 00:19:54,920
Spit it out.

466
00:19:56,520 --> 00:19:57,920
I'm not saying anything.

467
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:02,640
When I get killed by someone one day,

468
00:20:02,640 --> 00:20:03,400
you can also issue a letter of forgiveness.

469
00:20:03,400 --> 00:20:05,000
Just sell me for a good price.

470
00:20:27,680 --> 00:20:28,920
Thank you for today.

471
00:20:31,760 --> 00:20:34,760
But I feel that your emotions towards Zhao Deqing

472
00:20:35,040 --> 00:20:35,880
have, to some extent,

473
00:20:35,880 --> 00:20:37,940
affected your judgment on this case.

474
00:20:39,400 --> 00:20:40,720
How was I affected?

475
00:20:41,080 --> 00:20:43,760
Lady Justice holds a sword and scales.

476
00:20:44,800 --> 00:20:47,000
But why is she also wearing a blindfold?

477
00:20:50,600 --> 00:20:51,280
Of course.

478
00:20:51,280 --> 00:20:54,240
Outside of my professional scope, I understand you.

479
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:55,280
Okay.

480
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:57,640
The impartial Lawyer Li

481
00:20:57,640 --> 00:20:59,570
is starting to understand people.

482
00:21:00,440 --> 00:21:01,520
Okay, thank you.

483
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:03,530
Go back. I'm going back too.

484
00:21:03,960 --> 00:21:04,820
Go to bed early.

485
00:21:05,760 --> 00:21:06,360
Okay.

486
00:21:34,720 --> 00:21:36,200
Long, come eat.

487
00:21:36,400 --> 00:21:37,160
Okay.

488
00:21:37,840 --> 00:21:38,920
Come on. No, no.

489
00:21:39,040 --> 00:21:40,400
There's no rush. Let's eat first.

490
00:21:40,400 --> 00:21:41,680
Word by word.

491
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:44,060
Hurry up. Eat this to nourish your brain.

492
00:21:44,280 --> 00:21:45,160
What is this?

493
00:21:45,600 --> 00:21:46,520
Braised pig brain.

494
00:21:46,520 --> 00:21:48,920
Are you sure you want to use pig brain to nourish a human brain?

495
00:21:48,920 --> 00:21:50,050
You are what you eat.

496
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:51,800
Then you should nourish yours first.

497
00:21:51,800 --> 00:21:52,280
Hurry up.

498
00:21:52,280 --> 00:21:53,520
Eat it.

499
00:22:00,640 --> 00:22:01,970
Why does it taste so bad?

500
00:22:02,480 --> 00:22:03,640
I followed the recipe exactly.

501
00:22:03,640 --> 00:22:05,400
That's a recipe for disaster.

502
00:22:05,640 --> 00:22:06,240
I've lost my touch.

503
00:22:06,240 --> 00:22:06,720
Don't.

504
00:22:06,720 --> 00:22:07,760
Eat this instead. Come on.

505
00:22:07,760 --> 00:22:08,240
Okay, let's eat this.

506
00:22:08,240 --> 00:22:08,970
This is good.

507
00:22:14,920 --> 00:22:16,720
I have your brother Zhao Deqing.

508
00:22:16,960 --> 00:22:18,360
Come over and let's talk.

509
00:22:20,520 --> 00:22:22,000
I'll only wait for you until six.

510
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:23,260
I won't wait past that.

511
00:22:23,480 --> 00:22:24,540
You name the place.

512
00:22:37,040 --> 00:22:38,970
What are you doing? This is Daqing.

513
00:22:39,880 --> 00:22:41,320
Why the sack?

514
00:22:41,800 --> 00:22:43,400
Take the sack off. Let me see.

515
00:22:50,760 --> 00:22:51,640
Last time at the KTV,

516
00:22:51,640 --> 00:22:52,770
you ran pretty fast.

517
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:54,200
Enemies often cross paths.

518
00:22:54,200 --> 00:22:56,130
You fell into my hands again today.

519
00:22:57,760 --> 00:23:01,160
Today we'll settle both old and new scores.

520
00:23:01,200 --> 00:23:03,160
Alright, you're done beating him, right?

521
00:23:03,160 --> 00:23:04,840
Since you're done, I'll just take him away.

522
00:23:04,840 --> 00:23:06,770
You're just going to take him away?

523
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:08,530
If you can't teach him well,

524
00:23:09,120 --> 00:23:10,520
I'll teach him for you.

525
00:23:11,440 --> 00:23:13,240
Come, cut his Achilles tendons.

526
00:23:13,800 --> 00:23:14,600
Wait, wait.

527
00:23:16,240 --> 00:23:17,760
No, why did you call me here?

528
00:23:17,760 --> 00:23:18,840
Wasn't it to talk?

529
00:23:19,360 --> 00:23:20,400
Just tell me how much money you want.

530
00:23:20,400 --> 00:23:21,260
How much money?

531
00:23:22,360 --> 00:23:23,040
First,

532
00:23:24,800 --> 00:23:27,760
half of the Leyang freight line belongs to me from now on.

533
00:23:27,760 --> 00:23:28,760
You stay out of it.

534
00:23:29,360 --> 00:23:30,280
Fine, I'll give it to you.

535
00:23:30,280 --> 00:23:31,340
Straightforward.

536
00:23:31,560 --> 00:23:32,400
Second,

537
00:23:33,360 --> 00:23:36,820
when you smashed my head that day, the brothers were all there.

538
00:23:38,240 --> 00:23:39,760
How can I show my face?

539
00:23:41,360 --> 00:23:45,440
You didn't leash your dog well, so you have to take responsibility.

540
00:23:46,040 --> 00:23:47,840
Today, in front of the brothers,

541
00:23:49,280 --> 00:23:50,680
you will kneel before me.

542
00:23:52,760 --> 00:23:53,520
Whatever you do,

543
00:23:53,520 --> 00:23:55,040
don't go too far.

544
00:23:55,520 --> 00:23:57,120
Aren't you so loyal?

545
00:23:57,760 --> 00:23:59,690
You're the Eight Great Guardians?

546
00:24:03,720 --> 00:24:05,920
Cut both of his Achilles tendons for me.

547
00:24:06,760 --> 00:24:07,360
Alright, alright.

548
00:24:07,360 --> 00:24:08,280
I... I'll kneel.

549
00:24:08,280 --> 00:24:09,210
You can't kneel.

550
00:24:09,240 --> 00:24:10,040
Shut up.

551
00:24:10,640 --> 00:24:11,400
Let him go,

552
00:24:12,120 --> 00:24:13,720
then let my brother stand up,

553
00:24:14,080 --> 00:24:15,340
and I'll kneel for you.

554
00:24:20,400 --> 00:24:21,280
Come, stand up.

555
00:24:22,960 --> 00:24:24,280
Brother, you can't.

556
00:24:24,280 --> 00:24:24,880
Brother.

557
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:25,800
Brother.

558
00:24:27,360 --> 00:24:28,160
Brother.

559
00:24:37,880 --> 00:24:38,600
Deqing.

560
00:25:29,240 --> 00:25:29,760
Come in.

561
00:25:30,440 --> 00:25:31,040
Lawyer Li,

562
00:25:31,760 --> 00:25:33,040
you've been working hard lately.

563
00:25:33,040 --> 00:25:35,840
I ordered your favorite iced Americano.

564
00:25:36,480 --> 00:25:37,280
Thank you,

565
00:25:37,760 --> 00:25:40,440
but I don't drink Americanos anymore.

566
00:25:42,760 --> 00:25:43,600
Understood.

567
00:25:43,960 --> 00:25:45,290
You have a new favorite.

568
00:25:45,440 --> 00:25:47,360
You fell in love with something else.

569
00:25:47,360 --> 00:25:48,760
I just don't understand.

570
00:25:48,840 --> 00:25:50,920
How can you just stop drinking it like that?

571
00:25:50,920 --> 00:25:52,920
So you just stop loving it like that?

572
00:25:52,920 --> 00:25:53,440
No.

573
00:25:54,200 --> 00:25:56,000
What did the Americano do wrong?

574
00:25:56,120 --> 00:25:57,640
Doesn't it taste good?

575
00:25:57,960 --> 00:25:59,760
The Americano is innocent!

576
00:26:00,120 --> 00:26:01,520
Are you okay, Americano?

577
00:26:03,200 --> 00:26:04,600
Do you have nothing to do?

578
00:26:07,360 --> 00:26:08,880
Well, nothing.

579
00:26:09,120 --> 00:26:10,250
Go back to your work.

580
00:26:10,520 --> 00:26:11,600
I empathized with it.

581
00:26:11,600 --> 00:26:12,240
Come on.

582
00:26:13,240 --> 00:26:16,200
If you have nothing to do, take the Americano away.

583
00:26:24,680 --> 00:26:26,480
Is it a crime not to drink coffee?

584
00:26:33,320 --> 00:26:34,240
He has changed.

585
00:26:44,080 --> 00:26:44,810
You're here.

586
00:26:45,800 --> 00:26:46,640
Have a seat.

587
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:48,680
Well...

588
00:26:49,520 --> 00:26:51,960
Let me apologize to you first.

589
00:26:51,960 --> 00:26:53,960
I really didn't dare to skip it yesterday,

590
00:26:53,960 --> 00:26:56,120
so I didn't have time to tip you off.

591
00:26:56,640 --> 00:26:58,520
So, what do you want for lunch today?

592
00:26:58,520 --> 00:27:00,720
My treat. Order whatever you want. I...

593
00:27:01,600 --> 00:27:02,660
My treat. My treat.

594
00:27:03,600 --> 00:27:05,240
The miser is finally spending money.

595
00:27:05,240 --> 00:27:06,840
I'm usually pretty generous, aren't I?

596
00:27:06,840 --> 00:27:08,240
Order whatever you want.

597
00:27:10,760 --> 00:27:13,240
Alright, it's not entirely your fault.

598
00:27:13,440 --> 00:27:14,240
Indeed,

599
00:27:14,920 --> 00:27:17,320
there are some unclear points in this case.

600
00:27:18,600 --> 00:27:20,840
Jun really got through to you.

601
00:27:20,840 --> 00:27:22,440
How did he do it? I should learn from him.

602
00:27:22,440 --> 00:27:25,360
Do you know why Lady Justice wears a blindfold?

603
00:27:28,600 --> 00:27:30,060
She's afraid of the light.

604
00:27:30,200 --> 00:27:32,060
I'm really scared of you, really.

605
00:27:32,160 --> 00:27:33,960
To maintain impartiality.

606
00:27:34,880 --> 00:27:35,760
Uncle.

607
00:27:36,160 --> 00:27:37,560
Maintain impartiality.

608
00:27:37,880 --> 00:27:38,840
Jun is brilliant.

609
00:27:38,840 --> 00:27:39,500
Brilliant.

610
00:27:40,360 --> 00:27:41,040
Luo Zhi,

611
00:27:41,240 --> 00:27:42,600
how's the audit going?

612
00:27:43,760 --> 00:27:45,720
Miaomiao and I checked it carefully several times.

613
00:27:45,720 --> 00:27:47,200
Zhao Deqing's auto repair shop

614
00:27:47,200 --> 00:27:48,440
has been running for several years.

615
00:27:48,440 --> 00:27:50,120
There are more than 100,000 in the account.

616
00:27:50,120 --> 00:27:51,720
And his daily expenses are not much.

617
00:27:51,720 --> 00:27:53,250
He lives a very frugal life.

618
00:27:53,400 --> 00:27:55,960
Then why did Zhao Deqing attack Fu Xiaochen?

619
00:27:56,320 --> 00:27:57,960
Then we have to see if Fu Xiaochen

620
00:27:57,960 --> 00:27:59,560
was acting in self-defense.

621
00:27:59,720 --> 00:28:00,480
That's right.

622
00:28:00,480 --> 00:28:01,720
Should I let Jun know?

623
00:28:01,720 --> 00:28:02,760
Don't you dare.

624
00:28:02,760 --> 00:28:03,880
Then I won't.

625
00:28:04,760 --> 00:28:05,680
Zhao Deqing?

626
00:28:05,840 --> 00:28:07,600
He doesn't talk to any of the neighbors,

627
00:28:07,600 --> 00:28:08,920
and he looks fierce.

628
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:11,000
How would I know anything about him?

629
00:28:11,600 --> 00:28:13,080
He beat and scolded Fu Xiaochen.

630
00:28:13,080 --> 00:28:15,280
Several of us neighbors saw it at the time.

631
00:28:15,280 --> 00:28:17,540
Zhao Deqing must have pushed him too far.

632
00:28:17,720 --> 00:28:20,160
When that young man was taken away by the police,

633
00:28:20,160 --> 00:28:21,640
He kept muttering,

634
00:28:21,640 --> 00:28:22,840
I didn't mean it.

635
00:28:22,920 --> 00:28:23,880
Didn't mean it.

636
00:28:24,200 --> 00:28:26,040
I heard it loud and clear.

637
00:28:31,200 --> 00:28:32,400
Hello? What's wrong?

638
00:28:33,920 --> 00:28:34,720
What?

639
00:28:35,520 --> 00:28:37,720
Filing a complaint against me to the Bar Association?

640
00:28:37,720 --> 00:28:39,000
Xiao Longnv's dad

641
00:28:39,360 --> 00:28:40,480
took a bunch of thugs

642
00:28:40,480 --> 00:28:43,200
to my client's house to threaten them.

643
00:28:43,280 --> 00:28:45,240
This is absolutely outrageous.

644
00:28:45,840 --> 00:28:48,400
I apologize to your client on behalf of my dad.

645
00:28:49,000 --> 00:28:49,840
After all,

646
00:28:49,840 --> 00:28:52,680
my dad and the victim have been friends for years.

647
00:28:53,200 --> 00:28:53,840
I'm sorry.

648
00:28:53,840 --> 00:28:55,640
Do you think a simple sorry is enough?

649
00:28:55,640 --> 00:28:56,440
Let me ask you,

650
00:28:56,480 --> 00:28:58,640
did you go to my client's house

651
00:28:58,640 --> 00:28:59,640
to ask his parents for money?

652
00:28:59,640 --> 00:29:01,100
I wasn't asking for money.

653
00:29:01,360 --> 00:29:04,680
I was negotiating compensation on behalf of the victim's family.

654
00:29:04,680 --> 00:29:06,360
What right do you have to negotiate compensation?

655
00:29:06,360 --> 00:29:07,840
Let me be clear.

656
00:29:07,840 --> 00:29:10,640
The Fu family won't pay a single cent.

657
00:29:10,840 --> 00:29:12,880
No, we are both lawyers.

658
00:29:12,880 --> 00:29:14,440
We should both know

659
00:29:14,440 --> 00:29:16,720
how important this letter of forgiveness is

660
00:29:16,720 --> 00:29:17,800
for Fu Xiaochen's sentence reduction.

661
00:29:17,800 --> 00:29:20,000
Shouldn't our goals be the same?

662
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:21,720
What same goals?

663
00:29:22,040 --> 00:29:25,880
Zhao Deqing has been bullying and exploiting Fu Xiaochen.

664
00:29:26,400 --> 00:29:28,200
Fu Xiaochen worked for him.

665
00:29:28,200 --> 00:29:29,660
Not only did he not pay him,

666
00:29:29,720 --> 00:29:32,250
he also wanted the money he earned elsewhere.

667
00:29:32,280 --> 00:29:33,600
If he didn't give it, he'd get beaten.

668
00:29:33,600 --> 00:29:35,440
Fu Xiaochen couldn't take it anymore,

669
00:29:35,440 --> 00:29:36,720
so he had to fight back.

670
00:29:36,720 --> 00:29:38,600
That's called self-defense.

671
00:29:38,720 --> 00:29:39,440
And you,

672
00:29:40,040 --> 00:29:41,400
you asked for an exorbitant amount,

673
00:29:41,400 --> 00:29:43,480
trying to scam all his money.

674
00:29:44,120 --> 00:29:45,380
Who's scamming money?

675
00:29:45,480 --> 00:29:47,000
No, wait a minute.

676
00:29:47,280 --> 00:29:48,240
Did Fu Xiaochen tell you all this

677
00:29:48,240 --> 00:29:50,200
himself?

678
00:29:50,480 --> 00:29:52,040
Are you trying to trick me into a confession?

679
00:29:52,040 --> 00:29:54,640
The first instance of this case is in the Intermediate People's Court,

680
00:29:54,640 --> 00:29:57,640
which means it's a relatively serious criminal case.

681
00:29:57,640 --> 00:29:58,800
Fu Xiaochen is very likely

682
00:29:58,800 --> 00:30:01,130
to be sentenced to life in prison or death.

683
00:30:01,320 --> 00:30:03,640
Don't give me that nonsense.

684
00:30:03,640 --> 00:30:05,760
One of them is an ex-convict,

685
00:30:05,760 --> 00:30:08,640
and the other has been clean all his life.

686
00:30:08,640 --> 00:30:09,560
Who is more credible?

687
00:30:09,560 --> 00:30:11,040
Isn't it obvious?

688
00:30:11,040 --> 00:30:13,640
Since when do we judge cases based on criminal records?

689
00:30:13,640 --> 00:30:15,080
Are you a professional?

690
00:30:15,200 --> 00:30:16,240
I'm not a professional?

691
00:30:16,240 --> 00:30:17,600
I've been practicing law

692
00:30:17,600 --> 00:30:19,200
longer than you've been alive.

693
00:30:19,200 --> 00:30:20,000
Lawyers,

694
00:30:20,120 --> 00:30:21,000
calm down.

695
00:30:21,280 --> 00:30:22,640
Let's just solve the problem.

696
00:30:22,640 --> 00:30:24,400
Calm down, both of you.

697
00:30:24,600 --> 00:30:25,760
Yeah, calm down.

698
00:30:25,760 --> 00:30:27,160
I'm not angry at all.

699
00:30:27,160 --> 00:30:29,240
I don't know why they're so mad.

700
00:30:29,240 --> 00:30:30,370
What's the big deal?

701
00:30:32,880 --> 00:30:33,940
Xiaochen's uncle,

702
00:30:33,960 --> 00:30:35,040
if she harasses you again,

703
00:30:35,040 --> 00:30:36,160
just call me.

704
00:30:36,320 --> 00:30:37,240
As for Xiaochen's case,

705
00:30:37,240 --> 00:30:38,200
leave it to me.

706
00:30:38,200 --> 00:30:39,160
Don't worry.

707
00:30:39,360 --> 00:30:40,480
I guarantee there won't be any problems.

708
00:30:40,480 --> 00:30:42,480
I'll handle this perfectly for you.

709
00:30:42,600 --> 00:30:43,280
Sister Long.

710
00:30:43,280 --> 00:30:44,240
You're out.

711
00:30:44,400 --> 00:30:46,860
Is that the lawyer who complained about you?

712
00:30:47,880 --> 00:30:50,480
He looks like an enlarged version of the Beast.

713
00:30:51,000 --> 00:30:53,880
This Lawyer Qian is really a bit unreliable.

714
00:30:54,040 --> 00:30:55,960
Not only did he not seek forgiveness,

715
00:30:55,960 --> 00:30:58,620
but he also didn't let Fu Xiaochen plead guilty.

716
00:30:59,520 --> 00:31:01,120
Won't he get a heavy sentence then?

717
00:31:01,120 --> 00:31:03,240
I've seen many unscrupulous lawyers like him.

718
00:31:03,240 --> 00:31:05,280
He'll say anything just to make money.

719
00:31:05,280 --> 00:31:06,160
I guess he's just afraid

720
00:31:06,160 --> 00:31:07,280
that Fu Xiaochen's parents will pay the compensation,

721
00:31:07,280 --> 00:31:08,400
and he won't make any money.

722
00:31:08,400 --> 00:31:09,040
Director.

723
00:31:09,520 --> 00:31:11,320
I just got Zhao Deqing's call records.

724
00:31:11,320 --> 00:31:12,250
I looked closely

725
00:31:12,360 --> 00:31:14,800
and found that around the time Zhao Deqing was murdered,

726
00:31:14,800 --> 00:31:16,520
someone talked to him on the phone.

727
00:31:16,520 --> 00:31:18,600
And this number has appeared a few times before.

728
00:31:18,600 --> 00:31:18,800
Called number 15263.

729
00:31:18,760 --> 00:31:20,290
Called number 1872635489.

730
00:31:18,760 --> 00:31:19,640
Called number 1526374.

731
00:31:25,120 --> 00:31:26,040
Hello.

732
00:31:26,480 --> 00:31:28,680
I'm the lawyer representing Zhao Deqing's family.

733
00:31:28,680 --> 00:31:29,680
My surname is Xiao.

734
00:31:29,680 --> 00:31:32,080
I don't know him. You have the wrong number.

735
00:31:36,440 --> 00:31:38,400
There was a mechanic at Zhangjiadian

736
00:31:38,400 --> 00:31:39,720
who got killed recently.

737
00:31:39,720 --> 00:31:40,760
Did you guys know?

738
00:31:41,040 --> 00:31:41,440
I...

739
00:31:41,640 --> 00:31:43,240
He probably deserved it.

740
00:31:43,720 --> 00:31:44,880
I heard all about it.

741
00:31:45,400 --> 00:31:46,330
I don't think so.

742
00:31:49,840 --> 00:31:51,640
How do you know he deserved it when you don't even know what happened?

743
00:31:51,640 --> 00:31:53,600
The guy who got killed had been in prison before.

744
00:31:53,600 --> 00:31:55,200
How could he be a good person?

745
00:31:55,240 --> 00:31:56,440
It's karma.

746
00:31:56,440 --> 00:31:57,520
Stop talking nonsense.

747
00:31:57,520 --> 00:32:00,450
Keep your mouth shut if you don't know what happened.

748
00:32:00,800 --> 00:32:02,280
I wasn't talking about you.

749
00:32:02,280 --> 00:32:03,680
Why are you so mad?

750
00:32:03,960 --> 00:32:05,160
I know you and the dead guy

751
00:32:05,160 --> 00:32:06,640
came out of the same cell.

752
00:32:06,640 --> 00:32:09,640
People like you should keep a low profile.

753
00:32:09,720 --> 00:32:12,720
Otherwise, you're just social scum even when you die.

754
00:32:14,920 --> 00:32:15,880
Stop fighting.

755
00:32:17,360 --> 00:32:19,160
Stop it.

756
00:32:19,920 --> 00:32:20,840
About this matter,

757
00:32:20,840 --> 00:32:23,100
you guys should go back and think it over.

758
00:32:23,160 --> 00:32:24,290
Come back next time.

759
00:32:24,400 --> 00:32:25,680
If mediation fails again,

760
00:32:25,680 --> 00:32:27,400
we'll handle it by the book.

761
00:32:27,520 --> 00:32:28,160
Okay.

762
00:32:28,880 --> 00:32:30,140
Sorry for the trouble.

763
00:32:30,720 --> 00:32:31,560
Will do.

764
00:32:32,320 --> 00:32:32,960
Thank you.

765
00:32:32,960 --> 00:32:34,320
So what if you have a lawyer?

766
00:32:34,320 --> 00:32:36,200
I'll get one too and sue you to death.

767
00:32:36,200 --> 00:32:37,160
Of course you can.

768
00:32:37,160 --> 00:32:38,320
But let me give you a piece of advice.

769
00:32:38,320 --> 00:32:40,120
Legally, this is considered a mutual fight.

770
00:32:40,120 --> 00:32:41,720
If you keep holding onto this,

771
00:32:41,720 --> 00:32:43,400
you might face administrative detention.

772
00:32:43,400 --> 00:32:44,440
Then detain me.

773
00:32:44,600 --> 00:32:45,130
Alright.

774
00:32:45,680 --> 00:32:47,840
Mr. Xiao has already decided to quit his job.

775
00:32:47,840 --> 00:32:48,600
What?

776
00:32:48,760 --> 00:32:49,960
Are you planning to quit your job

777
00:32:49,960 --> 00:32:51,620
and keep him company in there?

778
00:32:56,960 --> 00:32:57,620
This act...

779
00:32:58,320 --> 00:32:59,920
I held back when I hit him.

780
00:32:59,920 --> 00:33:01,320
Otherwise, he would have been in the hospital.

781
00:33:01,320 --> 00:33:02,840
If he really went to the hospital,

782
00:33:02,840 --> 00:33:04,320
you wouldn't be standing here.

783
00:33:04,320 --> 00:33:04,920
Let's go.

784
00:33:05,360 --> 00:33:07,690
You're too old to be fighting all the time.

785
00:33:08,920 --> 00:33:09,680
Xiaoxin,

786
00:33:10,080 --> 00:33:11,080
thank you.

787
00:33:12,160 --> 00:33:13,220
This godfather...

788
00:33:15,160 --> 00:33:16,400
Why is there a door god here?

789
00:33:16,400 --> 00:33:17,960
Why did you bring your dad here?

790
00:33:17,960 --> 00:33:19,200
Let's go, Godfather.

791
00:33:20,880 --> 00:33:21,640
Thanks for your hard work.

792
00:33:21,640 --> 00:33:23,240
I'll leave Godfather to you.

793
00:33:24,600 --> 00:33:26,800
Are you two handing over a prisoner?

794
00:33:26,800 --> 00:33:28,730
Doing a point-to-point handover?

795
00:33:30,800 --> 00:33:32,080
I... I'll open the door.

796
00:33:32,080 --> 00:33:32,680
Open it.

797
00:33:37,480 --> 00:33:38,880
What are you doing?

798
00:33:38,880 --> 00:33:39,480
Go in.

799
00:33:57,680 --> 00:33:59,560
No, you don't have to stay here with me.

800
00:33:59,560 --> 00:34:00,960
Look how old I am.

801
00:34:00,960 --> 00:34:01,680
Where else can I go?

802
00:34:01,680 --> 00:34:02,680
What else can I do?

803
00:34:03,320 --> 00:34:03,920
You... you should...

804
00:34:03,920 --> 00:34:05,980
Shouldn't you go home and take a look?

805
00:34:12,120 --> 00:34:13,159
Report, officer.

806
00:34:13,400 --> 00:34:14,199
What is it now?

807
00:34:14,320 --> 00:34:14,920
I'm hungry.

808
00:34:14,920 --> 00:34:15,800
I need to eat.

809
00:34:15,800 --> 00:34:18,080
I can't afford to waste time with you, you know?

810
00:34:18,080 --> 00:34:19,600
I... you... you...

811
00:34:19,600 --> 00:34:21,800
Staying here is really... honestly...

812
00:34:29,120 --> 00:34:29,880
I...

813
00:34:30,679 --> 00:34:32,679
Why do I have to eat instant noodles?

814
00:34:32,840 --> 00:34:33,679
Just make do with it.

815
00:34:33,679 --> 00:34:35,880
Eating instant noodles all the time is bad for my health.

816
00:34:35,880 --> 00:34:36,400
I want to cook.

817
00:34:36,400 --> 00:34:38,130
I want to stir-fry some dishes.

818
00:34:39,159 --> 00:34:40,679
If you want to cook, we have to do it together.

819
00:34:40,679 --> 00:34:41,400
Alright, alright.

820
00:34:41,400 --> 00:34:42,600
Let's do it together.

821
00:34:42,679 --> 00:34:44,409
Let me tell you what dish... no.

822
00:34:44,600 --> 00:34:46,199
The food is over there, look.

823
00:34:48,239 --> 00:34:48,960
Xiao Jun,

824
00:34:49,760 --> 00:34:50,760
open the door for me.

825
00:34:50,760 --> 00:34:52,159
Xiao Jun, open the door.

826
00:34:52,760 --> 00:34:53,889
Open the door for me.

827
00:34:55,400 --> 00:34:56,239
Open it for me.

828
00:34:56,239 --> 00:34:58,240
Open the door for me.

829
00:34:59,240 --> 00:35:00,600
I'll count to three.

830
00:35:01,120 --> 00:35:01,880
Xiao Jun.

831
00:35:24,640 --> 00:35:25,960
Don't worry, Dad Li.

832
00:35:25,960 --> 00:35:27,000
I found him.

833
00:35:33,720 --> 00:35:34,320
Pause.

834
00:35:37,120 --> 00:35:37,920
What is this?

835
00:35:38,560 --> 00:35:39,880
Zoom in a little more.

836
00:35:40,920 --> 00:35:41,850
What does it say?

837
00:35:42,120 --> 00:35:42,680
Bai...

838
00:35:42,760 --> 00:35:43,720
Baihe.

839
00:35:43,920 --> 00:35:44,920
Baihe Hair Salon.

840
00:35:48,040 --> 00:35:49,120
Baihe.

841
00:35:51,920 --> 00:35:52,720
The haircutting skills

842
00:35:52,720 --> 00:35:53,560
are really good.

843
00:35:53,560 --> 00:35:54,680
Isn't this the phone number

844
00:35:54,680 --> 00:35:56,480
from Zhao Deqing's last call?

845
00:36:03,280 --> 00:36:04,880
Is your name Zheng Xiaohong?

846
00:36:06,280 --> 00:36:08,480
You left this fingerprint, didn't you?

847
00:36:09,280 --> 00:36:10,520
Do I have to get a forensic appraisal

848
00:36:10,520 --> 00:36:11,840
before you admit it?

849
00:36:12,280 --> 00:36:13,840
I don't mean anything else.

850
00:36:13,840 --> 00:36:14,880
Just tell me,

851
00:36:14,880 --> 00:36:17,200
what's your relationship with Zhao Deqing?

852
00:36:17,200 --> 00:36:18,960
My child needs to eat.

853
00:36:19,200 --> 00:36:20,720
Please leave.

854
00:36:21,400 --> 00:36:22,000
No, don't.

855
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:23,120
Leave. Tell me.

856
00:36:23,280 --> 00:36:24,320
Leave.

857
00:36:24,800 --> 00:36:25,200
You...

858
00:36:25,920 --> 00:36:28,120
If you pull me again, I'm telling you...

859
00:36:28,320 --> 00:36:29,880
What exactly do you want?

860
00:36:30,080 --> 00:36:32,520
I told you I don't know any Zhao Deqing.

861
00:36:33,120 --> 00:36:33,880
What's wrong with you?

862
00:36:33,880 --> 00:36:35,320
Are you going to stab me?

863
00:36:36,240 --> 00:36:37,040
My God, she...

864
00:36:39,240 --> 00:36:40,500
What's wrong with you?

865
00:36:42,240 --> 00:36:43,000
Are you trying to kill someone?

866
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:43,800
Xiao Jun.

867
00:36:44,080 --> 00:36:44,560
You...

868
00:36:46,240 --> 00:36:47,300
What are you doing?

869
00:36:48,080 --> 00:36:49,540
You even brought a weapon.

870
00:36:49,760 --> 00:36:50,560
What are you doing?

871
00:36:50,560 --> 00:36:52,120
I...

872
00:36:52,440 --> 00:36:53,880
The scissors were in her hand just now.

873
00:36:53,880 --> 00:36:54,920
She was going to stab me.

874
00:36:54,920 --> 00:36:56,380
I wasn't going to stab her.

875
00:36:57,920 --> 00:36:59,240
Let the child speak.

876
00:36:59,240 --> 00:37:01,370
Weren't they in her hand just now? I...

877
00:37:04,440 --> 00:37:05,280
That's enough.

878
00:37:05,280 --> 00:37:06,680
Come with me, Jun.

879
00:37:07,120 --> 00:37:07,880
How embarrassing.

880
00:37:07,880 --> 00:37:09,880
You're holding scissors and you...

881
00:37:10,080 --> 00:37:10,880
No, no, no.

882
00:37:11,240 --> 00:37:12,360
Stop it.

883
00:37:12,360 --> 00:37:13,760
People are scared of you.

884
00:37:14,440 --> 00:37:15,080
Um...

885
00:37:16,600 --> 00:37:17,520
I'm sorry.

886
00:37:31,320 --> 00:37:33,000
Actually, I saw you that day

887
00:37:33,240 --> 00:37:34,570
at the auto repair shop.

888
00:37:34,880 --> 00:37:36,540
You were wearing blue, right?

889
00:37:42,160 --> 00:37:43,820
Our investigation found that

890
00:37:43,880 --> 00:37:45,080
when Zhao Deqing's incident happened,

891
00:37:45,080 --> 00:37:46,740
you were on the phone with him.

892
00:37:46,760 --> 00:37:48,560
So we just wanted to come and ask.

893
00:37:50,600 --> 00:37:53,000
I really didn't hear anything on that call.

894
00:37:53,560 --> 00:37:55,290
There was no signal at the time.

895
00:37:55,320 --> 00:37:56,800
I already told the police.

896
00:37:56,920 --> 00:37:58,840
Don't worry. Even if you heard something,

897
00:37:58,840 --> 00:38:01,840
it absolutely won't affect you. Really.

898
00:38:07,000 --> 00:38:09,200
If there's nothing else, please leave.

899
00:38:15,360 --> 00:38:16,520
What did I say?

900
00:38:16,680 --> 00:38:17,920
I told him he was that kind of person,

901
00:38:17,920 --> 00:38:19,240
but my dad wouldn't believe it.

902
00:38:19,240 --> 00:38:20,440
He insisted I investigate.

903
00:38:20,440 --> 00:38:22,840
What could I possibly find out? Seriously.

904
00:38:24,800 --> 00:38:26,530
Sister, don't misunderstand.

905
00:38:26,840 --> 00:38:28,170
That was my dad just now.

906
00:38:28,360 --> 00:38:30,920
He and Zhao Deqing were sworn brothers.

907
00:38:31,080 --> 00:38:32,400
They even went to prison together

908
00:38:32,400 --> 00:38:33,800
and roamed the world together.

909
00:38:33,800 --> 00:38:35,240
Now that he knows Uncle Deqing is gone,

910
00:38:35,240 --> 00:38:36,440
he really can't take it.

911
00:38:36,440 --> 00:38:38,000
So he insisted I come over to investigate,

912
00:38:38,000 --> 00:38:39,440
saying he just wants the truth.

913
00:38:39,440 --> 00:38:41,320
Don't I know Uncle Deqing?

914
00:38:41,560 --> 00:38:43,320
He's fighting and killing every day,

915
00:38:43,320 --> 00:38:45,160
stabbing someone or hitting another.

916
00:38:45,160 --> 00:38:47,360
Even his own sister knows what kind of person he is.

917
00:38:47,360 --> 00:38:49,360
The truth is he deserved it.

918
00:38:49,560 --> 00:38:50,680
To put it bluntly,

919
00:38:50,680 --> 00:38:52,160
Uncle Deqing ending up like this

920
00:38:52,160 --> 00:38:53,800
is just heaven punishing the wicked.

921
00:38:53,800 --> 00:38:55,240
He deserved to be stabbed.

922
00:38:55,240 --> 00:38:56,640
Sister, don't you agree?

923
00:38:58,280 --> 00:38:59,280
What's there to investigate?

924
00:38:59,280 --> 00:39:00,480
Okay, that's it.

925
00:39:01,840 --> 00:39:03,120
It's not like that.

926
00:39:09,200 --> 00:39:11,330
Zhao Deqing is not that kind of person.

927
00:39:22,080 --> 00:39:23,760
I only met Daqing

928
00:39:24,320 --> 00:39:25,840
because of Fu Xiaochen.

929
00:39:34,480 --> 00:39:36,200
Um, hello.

930
00:39:37,320 --> 00:39:38,640
Is this bag yours?

931
00:39:42,760 --> 00:39:43,480
Take a look

932
00:39:43,760 --> 00:39:45,490
and see if anything is missing.

933
00:39:58,280 --> 00:39:59,000
Well,

934
00:40:00,880 --> 00:40:02,540
could you not call the police?

935
00:40:02,680 --> 00:40:04,560
It's the kid's first time doing such a shameful thing.

936
00:40:04,560 --> 00:40:05,890
Just spare him this once

937
00:40:05,920 --> 00:40:08,580
and give him a chance to be a decent person, okay?

938
00:40:13,000 --> 00:40:13,760
Thank you.

939
00:40:16,880 --> 00:40:17,560
Wait.

940
00:40:20,920 --> 00:40:21,920
What else?

941
00:40:23,560 --> 00:40:26,400
Since you helped me get this bag back,

942
00:40:27,800 --> 00:40:29,600
let me trim your hair for you.

943
00:40:41,200 --> 00:40:42,400
Is this your child?

944
00:40:44,360 --> 00:40:45,960
What's wrong with the child?

945
00:40:49,440 --> 00:40:50,770
Prenatal brain damage.

946
00:40:51,120 --> 00:40:52,320
He was born like this.

947
00:40:55,160 --> 00:40:56,840
He heard that the child's father

948
00:40:56,840 --> 00:40:58,640
ran away right after he was born.

949
00:40:59,400 --> 00:41:00,360
Since then,

950
00:41:00,560 --> 00:41:01,880
he's been coming over every now and then

951
00:41:01,880 --> 00:41:03,960
to bring us some food and drinks.

952
00:41:05,480 --> 00:41:06,080
Xiaohong.

953
00:41:06,600 --> 00:41:07,480
I'm here.

954
00:41:08,000 --> 00:41:09,000
Here, some stuff.

955
00:41:09,880 --> 00:41:10,920
Where's the child?

956
00:41:10,920 --> 00:41:11,800
Asleep.

957
00:41:13,600 --> 00:41:15,920
Brother, don't trouble yourself.

958
00:41:16,120 --> 00:41:17,280
You haven't eaten yet, right?

959
00:41:17,280 --> 00:41:18,800
I just cooked some noodles.

960
00:41:18,800 --> 00:41:20,200
Come, eat while it's hot.

961
00:41:31,880 --> 00:41:32,760
Daqing.

962
00:41:34,520 --> 00:41:36,180
I've always wanted to ask you,

963
00:41:36,560 --> 00:41:38,920
about the scar on your face.

964
00:41:40,200 --> 00:41:41,460
It wasn't from a fight.

965
00:41:42,360 --> 00:41:44,960
When I was driving a truck back then,

966
00:41:45,600 --> 00:41:47,880
I almost died in a crash.

967
00:41:48,240 --> 00:41:50,080
The truck was completely totaled.

968
00:41:50,080 --> 00:41:51,480
I was knocked dizzy at the time,

969
00:41:51,480 --> 00:41:52,480
covered in blood.

970
00:41:53,000 --> 00:41:54,400
A sworn brother of mine

971
00:41:55,680 --> 00:41:58,200
ran all the way to the hospital with me on his back,

972
00:41:58,200 --> 00:41:59,240
and saved my life.

973
00:42:00,720 --> 00:42:02,980
A step later and I would have met my maker.

974
00:42:03,600 --> 00:42:05,000
Later, this brother of mine

975
00:42:05,000 --> 00:42:06,330
got the guys in the fleet

976
00:42:06,560 --> 00:42:08,360
to chip in and buy me a used truck.

977
00:42:09,720 --> 00:42:11,720
I continued to haul goods with them.

978
00:42:12,240 --> 00:42:13,480
It was only later that I found out

979
00:42:13,480 --> 00:42:14,520
that the money for the truck,

980
00:42:14,520 --> 00:42:16,980
more than half of it was paid by that brother.

981
00:42:18,080 --> 00:42:20,810
I owe him a debt I can never repay in this lifetime.

982
00:42:23,080 --> 00:42:25,240
Once, when we didn't have enough for the child's medical bills,

983
00:42:25,240 --> 00:42:27,440
he even helped by fronting 20,000 yuan.

984
00:42:27,920 --> 00:42:29,580
He absolutely refused an IOU.

985
00:42:29,760 --> 00:42:31,520
As for the IOU you saw,

986
00:42:31,560 --> 00:42:33,820
I secretly slipped it into his notebook.

987
00:42:34,480 --> 00:42:36,320
The time I went to deliver the IOU,

988
00:42:36,320 --> 00:42:39,800
I even saw Brother Daqing teaching Fu Xiaochen how to fix cars.

989
00:42:39,800 --> 00:42:41,400
Uncle, this is too hard.

990
00:42:41,720 --> 00:42:42,720
What isn't hard?

991
00:42:43,200 --> 00:42:45,320
You're a young man with no diploma.

992
00:42:45,400 --> 00:42:46,280
If you don't learn a skill,

993
00:42:46,280 --> 00:42:48,040
how will you support yourself in the future?

994
00:42:48,040 --> 00:42:51,570
Then how did they end up like this when they were perfectly fine?

995
00:42:52,440 --> 00:42:56,720
Then, what exactly did you hear on that phone call?
